WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.947
MyCampusView Academy.

2
00:00:02.997 --> 00:00:06.486
AI for Young Builders, video 7.

3
00:00:06.536 --> 00:00:09.910
Testing: is your AI any good?.

4
00:00:11.050 --> 00:00:15.320
A model that only works on the examples it was trained on

5
00:00:15.370 --> 00:00:19.261
is like a student who memorised last year’s answers.

6
00:00:19.311 --> 00:00:21.080
Let us test it properly.

7
00:00:22.450 --> 00:00:24.620
Keep some examples back.

8
00:00:24.670 --> 00:00:26.284
Train on the rest.

9
00:00:26.334 --> 00:00:31.556
Then test on the ones the model has never seen, just like

10
00:00:31.606 --> 00:00:33.960
an exam has new questions.

11
00:00:34.010 --> 00:00:35.810
That is a fair test.

12
00:00:37.150 --> 00:00:41.343
Accuracy is the share of test examples it gets right.

13
00:00:41.393 --> 00:00:46.628
Sixteen right out of twenty is sixteen divided by twenty, which is

14
00:00:46.678 --> 00:00:49.510
zero point eight, or eighty percent.

15
00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:55.058
Accuracy does not say which mistakes it makes.

16
00:00:55.108 --> 00:00:57.280
A confusion matrix does.

17
00:00:57.330 --> 00:01:02.187
Rows are the real answer, columns are the prediction.

18
00:01:02.237 --> 00:01:05.612
The diagonal shows the right answers.

19
00:01:05.662 --> 00:01:09.685
Here, two squares were mistaken for circles.

20
00:01:09.735 --> 00:01:12.740
Now you know exactly what to fix.

21
00:01:14.050 --> 00:01:17.881
In this lesson you can also train with your camera.

22
00:01:17.931 --> 00:01:22.295
Pictures are shrunk to a tiny twelve by nine grid and used

23
00:01:22.345 --> 00:01:23.893
only inside the page.

24
00:01:23.943 --> 00:01:30.210
Lighting changes the pixel numbers, so give your model examples in different light.

25
00:01:31.550 --> 00:01:33.451
Be a model doctor.

26
00:01:33.501 --> 00:01:37.462
Perfect on training but poor on test?

27
00:01:37.512 --> 00:01:40.606
It memorised, so add variety.

28
00:01:40.656 --> 00:01:42.991
One group often wrong?

29
00:01:43.041 --> 00:01:45.593
Add more examples of it.

30
00:01:45.643 --> 00:01:47.653
Fails in new light?

31
00:01:47.703 --> 00:01:50.255
Train in that light too.

32
00:01:50.305 --> 00:01:53.290
Then retrain and test again.

33
00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:56.036
Let us recap.

34
00:01:56.086 --> 00:02:00.191
Test on examples the model has never seen.

35
00:02:00.241 --> 00:02:03.753
Accuracy is the share it gets right.

36
00:02:03.803 --> 00:02:08.798
A confusion matrix shows which groups get mixed up.

37
00:02:08.848 --> 00:02:13.250
Next: Decision trees: AI that asks questions.
